-- title:
--   Rankin–Selberg unfolding on a determinant slab for GL₂
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field with adele ring $\mathbb{A}$, and let $\alpha$ be the character of $\mathbb{A}^\times$ obtained from the distributive Haar character of $\mathbb{A}$ composed with $\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}\to\mathbb{R}$, assumed everywhere positive. Fix carrier data: a set $D\subseteq\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$, a family $U$ of subgroups indexed by ideals of $\mathcal{O}_F$ and a family $\mathrm{gen}$ indexed by the height-one primes; these are assembled by `productionPinsOf` together with Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$, the full subgroup $Z=\top$ of $\mathbb{A}^\times$, and the adelic Haar measure conditioned on the box `adelicBox F`, the last being the measure used in Whittaker coefficients: $W_a(z)(g)=\int z(n(u)g)\,\psi(-(au))\,du$ over the conditioned box measure. Let $\psi$ be a global additive character (continuous, nontrivial, trivial on $F$), let $\mu,\nu$ be characters of $\mathbb{A}^\times$ that are unitary and trivial on $F^\times$, let $s\in\mathbb{C}$, and let $\varphi:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})\to\mathbb{C}$ be continuous and an induced section for the pair $(\mu\,\alpha^{s+1/2},\,\nu\,\alpha^{-(s+1/2)})$, i.e. $\varphi(bg)=\mu\alpha^{s+1/2}(b_{11})\,\nu\alpha^{-(s+1/2)}(b_{22})\,\varphi(g)$ for $b$ upper triangular, with $\sum_{\xi\in F}\|\varphi(w\,n(\xi)g)\|<\infty$ for every $g$, where $w$ is the adelic Weyl element. Let $x,y:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})\to\mathbb{C}$ be continuous and invariant under left translation by $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$, with $W_0(x)(g)=0$ and $\sum_{a\in F}\|W_a(x)(g)\|<\infty$ for all $g$. Let $w\in\mathbb{R}$ (the exponent), $0<d_1<d_2$, and let $\mathcal{F}$ be a subset of the slab $X=\{g:\|\det g\|_{\mathbb{A}}\in[d_1,d_2]\}$ which is a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ acting on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$ with respect to Haar measure restricted to $X$; assume that $g\mapsto\|x(g)\|^2\bigl(\|\varphi(g)\|+\sum_{\xi}\|\varphi(w n(\xi)g)\|\bigr)\|\det g\|^{-w}$ and its analogue with $y$ are integrable on $\mathcal{F}$. Then, with $H=Z(F)\cdot N(\mathbb{A})$ the subgroup generated by the rational centre and the adelic unipotent subgroup and $Q=H\backslash\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$ carrying the quotient measure `rationalCentreUnipotentQuotientMeasure F`, the function $$q\mapsto \mathbf{1}_X(q^{\mathrm{out}})\,W_1(x)(q^{\mathrm{out}})\,\overline{W_1(y)(q^{\mathrm{out}})}\,\varphi(q^{\mathrm{out}})\,\|\det q^{\mathrm{out}}\|^{-w}$$ on representatives $q^{\mathrm{out}}$ is integrable on $Q$, and the Petersson integral $\int_{\mathcal{F}} x(g)E(g)\,\overline{y(g)}\,\|\det g\|^{-w}\,dg$, where $E(g)=\varphi(g)+\sum_{\xi\in F}\varphi(w\,n(\xi)g)$, equals its integral over $Q$.
--
--   This is the Rankin–Selberg unfolding step for $\mathrm{GL}_2\times\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a number field, carried out on a slab $d_1\le\|\det\|\le d_2$ rather than modulo the centre, and ending on the homogeneous space $Z(F)N(\mathbb{A})\backslash\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A})$, where the two Whittaker coefficients at $1$ appear paired against the inducing section $\varphi$. It feeds the construction of test data for the analytic continuation of the Rankin–Selberg integral and its Euler factorisation.
